  "body": "The [strictly splitting algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#strictly-split-a-string) is not the inverse of joining, which is the behavior of string splitting of most programming languages. \r\nChanging the algorithm would align it with the assumptions made by the [CSP specification](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#match-paths), and likely other consumers. \r\n\r\nFor example, for two inputs of `/a/` and `/a` and a delimiter character `/`, current algorithm produces the same token list of `[\"\", \"a\"]` and *discards* the information about second delimiter.\r\n\r\nProposed algorithm for the same input produces two distinct token lists:\r\n`/a/` -> `[\"\", \"a\", \"\"]`\r\n`/a` -> `[\"\", \"a\"]`\r\n\r\nI'll be sending a pull request shortly. \r\n",
